criteria":["E4"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.25,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'normalize complete `name`, `description`, and `isRequired` records from the canonical inventory'","src/rebar/mcp_server.py:111-160: each MCP_ENV_VARS entry has keys `name`, `description`, `deprecated` — no `isRequired`","scripts/check_server_manifest.py:25: regeneration one-liner hardcodes `\"isRequired\": False`","server.json lines 24-199: every record is `\"isRequired\": false` (uniform constant)"],"finding":"The plan asserts it will normalize `isRequired` records 'from the canonical inventory' (`rebar.mcp_server.MCP_ENV_VARS`), but MCP_ENV_VARS entries carry no `isRequired` key — only `name`, `description`, and `deprecated`. server.json hardcodes `isRequired: false` uniformly, and the existing checker's regeneration one-liner sets it as a literal `False`. The plan's premise that `isRequired` is sourced from the canonical inventory is refuted by the code, leaving the `isRequired` comparison's source of truth unspecified.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f76b1532f96eb3dcf","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan section 'Plan', first bullet; Acceptance Criteria line 'An isRequired mismatch causes a nonzero checker result'","norm_id":"n589476c77b6ecc3f","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer tries to read `v[\"isRequired\"]` from MCP_ENV_VARS and hits a KeyError","Reviewer cannot tell whether the checker should compare against a constant `False`, a new MCP_ENV_VARS field, or a derived value"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify how the canonical `isRequired` value is sourced, given MCP_ENV_VARS records carry only name/description/deprecated (e.g., add an `isRequired` field to MCP_ENV_VARS, or define the canonical value as a constant `False`/derived-from-`deprecated`), and reconcile with all records in server.json currently being `isRequired: false`.","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.3,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'normalize complete `name`, `description`, and `isRequired` records from the canonical inventory and `server.json`.'","src/rebar/mcp_server.py:111-179 — every MCP_ENV_VARS record has keys name/description/deprecated only","search_files for 'isRequired' in mcp_server.py returns (no matches); 'required' matches are only prose in descriptions, not a record key","server.json records all hardcode 'isRequired': false (server.json:24,29,...) so there is no per-var required signal on either side to compare"],"finding":"The plan says the checker will 'normalize complete name, description, and isRequired records from the canonical inventory,' but rebar.mcp_server.MCP_ENV_VARS entries expose only name/description/deprecated — there is no isRequired (nor required/is_required) key on the canonical records, so the plan names a field on the canonical side that does not exist and never specifies how the canonical isRequired value is derived.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fab75a13bbc6ac7f9","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan section 'Plan', first bullet; AC line 'An isRequired mismatch causes a nonzero checker result'","norm_id":"nf7bca7158e391677","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer tries to read v['isRequired'] from MCP_ENV_VARS and hits a KeyError","isRequired comparison is silently no-op'd against a hardcoded False, making the 'isRequired mismatch -> nonzero' AC untestable against the real canonical inventory"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Either extend MCP_ENV_VARS to include an explicit per-var isRequired key (updating the canonical tuple in src/rebar/mcp_server.py), or state in the plan that the canonical isRequired is the constant False for every var (matching today's server.json) and have the checker assert server.json never sets isRequired:true; whichever is chosen, make the 'isRequired mismatch' AC exercise it explicitly.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silen